<Project>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!--
      GHSA-2m69-gcr7-jv3q (CVE-2025-6965): SQLitePCLRaw.lib.e_sqlite3 2.1.11 bundles a native SQLite
      (3.49.1) affected by a memory-corruption bug that is only reachable by executing crafted SQL text
      against the SQLite engine. It is pulled in transitively by Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Sqlite and
      the package is deprecated with NO patched release available for net10.0 (the successor
      SourceGear.sqlite3 has no net10.0 build assets yet and ships static libs for Linux, so it does not
      cleanly replace the loaded shared library). Tracked upstream in dotnet/efcore#38257.

      This is suppressed rather than force-patched because it is not reachable in this application:
        * SQLite is used ONLY by EF Core for the manager's own metadata database, with fully parameterized,
          EF-generated queries. There are no FromSqlRaw/ExecuteSqlRaw call sites and no user-supplied raw
          SQL reaches SQLite.
        * The attacker-facing database (AzerothCore accounts/characters) is MySQL - a completely separate
          engine - accessed via parameterized Dapper/EF queries.
      Re-evaluate and remove this suppression once EF Core ships a Sqlite provider that depends on a
      non-vulnerable native SQLite (or a net10.0-compatible SourceGear.sqlite3 becomes available).
    -->
    <NuGetAuditSuppress Include="https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-2m69-gcr7-jv3q" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
